[SIZE="4"][B]RPQuest[/B][/SIZE]
A native, [B]zero-dependency[/B] add-on for [B]The Elder Scrolls Online[/B] that lets you create, play, complete, and share [B]custom Roleplay quests[/B] directly inside ESO's native UI.

[SIZE="3"][B]Key Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Native Quest Journal Integration (J):[/B] Adds a dedicated [B]RPQuest[/B] tab inside the standard Quest Journal with separate [B]Prepared[/B] (authored) and [B]Received[/B] (active/playable) quest lists.
[*][B]Reticle NPC Target Capture:[/B] Aim at any living NPC and press your keybind to register objectives automatically. Capturing the same NPC name multiple times stacks into [I]Imp x3[/I]; different named NPCs are tracked individually.
[*][B]Hidden Discovery Points:[/B] Capture in-world exploration coordinates with configurable trigger radii ([I]Small[/I], [I]Medium[/I], [I]Large[/I]) without cluttering the map or compass with spoilers.
[*][B]Optional Stealth / Undetected Condition:[/B] Require players to complete objectives without being detected in combat.
[*][B]World Map Search Area (M):[/B] Displays an approximate search circle on the World Map using a deterministic, fixed random offset—keeping the target inside the circle without revealing its exact center. Automatically clears upon completion or deactivation.
[*][B]Native NPC Dialogue Injection:[/B] Bind custom RPQuest dialogue lines to native ESO NPCs (via reticle capture or NPC name), injected seamlessly into the native interaction window without altering original NPC options.
[*][B]Combat & Discovery Tracking + Native Alerts:[/B] Tracks kills and exploration proximity, triggering native Center Screen Announcements (including when accepting a shared quest by code) and official quest sounds.
[*][B]HUD Mini-Tracker:[/B] Displays the active custom quest on the side of your screen (left-click opens the Journal; right-click centers the World Map on the search area).
[*][B]Code Sharing & Completion Proof (RPQ2 / RPQC1):[/B] Export any prepared quest as a compact, checksum-verified share code for other players to import, and generate a delivery validation code upon completion to prove it back to the Quest Master.
[*][B]Per-Character Persistence & Auto-Localization:[/B] Stores progress per character via SavedVariables and auto-detects client language (English / Spanish).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Keybinds (Settings -> Controls -> RPQuest)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Capture Target under Reticle:[/B] Captures the living NPC currently under your reticle into the quest draft.
[*][B]Capture Discovery Point:[/B] Captures your current character position as a hidden discovery objective.
[*][B]Toggle Custom Quests Tab:[/B] Opens or closes the Quest Journal directly on the [B]RPQuest[/B] tab.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Quick Start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Create a Quest:[/B] Open the Quest Journal ([B]J[/B]), switch to the [B]RPQuest[/B] tab, and click [B]Create Quest[/B]. Use the collapsible sections to set Title, Description, Search Area size, optional Stealth condition, and optional NPC Dialogue lines. Aim at NPCs or stand at discovery spots and press your keybinds.
[*][B]Share with Players:[/B] Select your prepared quest and copy its share code. Players paste that code into the [B]Import[/B] field in their [B]RPQuest[/B] tab. Note: quest codes require the same game client language as the creator—ESO does not expose universal NPC IDs across locales, and changing languages directly would prevent NPC objectives and dialogues from matching.
[*][B]Play & Verify:[/B] Activate the received quest to show the HUD mini-tracker and World Map search area. Once completed, copy the generated delivery code to confirm completion.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]External Libraries:[/B] None (Zero-Dependency)
[*][B]Languages:[/B] English (en), Spanish (es)
[/LIST]
